+## Acceptance
+
+- `skills/design/scripts/revise-plan-with-waterfall.sh` exists, sources `lib-quiet.sh`, and accepts the documented argv (preflight rejects mismatched `--plan-file` with exit 2).
+- The Codex → Cursor → Claude waterfall runs with `--prompt-file` as the sole prompt source; no `--description-text` is forwarded.
+- Unified-diff patches with non-`a/plan.txt` / `b/plan.txt` headers are rejected before `git apply --check`; no `--unsafe-paths` is used.
+- Plan snapshot at `<plan-file>.before-revise` is taken before any tier runs, restored on validation/apply/heading/emit-plan failure, and removed only on overall success.
+- Post-apply heading check restores the plan when a revision drops every `### NEW/UPDATED/REWRITTEN` heading from a plan that originally had at least one.
+- The emit-plan gate (`ACTION=EMIT_PLAN`) is the final structural validator; failure reverts the plan via the snapshot.
+- All KV keys (`REVISE_STATUS`, `REVISE_TIER`, `REVISE_PATCH_PATH`, `REVISE_PLAN_HASH_BEFORE`, `REVISE_PLAN_HASH_AFTER`, `REVISE_TIER_1_STATUS`/`_2_`/`_3_`) are emitted on every invocation; failure paths emit explicit empty values for `REVISE_TIER` and `REVISE_PATCH_PATH`.
+- Per-tier ordinal mapping is documented in the sibling `.md`: `REVISE_TIER_1_STATUS`=codex, `REVISE_TIER_2_STATUS`=cursor, `REVISE_TIER_3_STATUS`=claude.
+- Codex/Cursor/Claude launcher invocations include `--timeout "$timeout"`.
+- `scripts/test-revise-plan-with-waterfall.sh` covers the 11 documented cases (Codex-wins, Cursor-wins, Claude-wins, all-fail, apply-failed, emit-plan-failed, codex-absent, argv-defect, canonical-plan invariant violation, heading-loss revert, launcher-prompt-source assertion); harness is fully mocked.
+- Sibling `.md` files exist for both the primary script and the harness, satisfying the `script-md-siblings` rule.
+- `Makefile` registers `test-revise-plan-with-waterfall` in `.PHONY:`, in `test-harnesses-9`, and as its own rule.
+- `make lint-bash32`, `make test-revise-plan-with-waterfall`, and `make test-harnesses-9` all pass.
